.ENDS

*-1) Open a command box in the loadflow_transient directory
*0) Run tinyperl gen_template_cable.pl -sys:1 (or 2) > template
*1) Run RunATP of the cable model input box
*2) copy Impedance-Matrix to Mat_L.txt
*3) note the capacitance of Conductor and Shield in the capacitance matrix
*4) Run Verify in the cable model input box
*5) note R conductor and Rshield
*6) Run tinyperl gen_lc_cable.pl > out
*7) Copy XL-matrix in out-file to the template at the right position
*8) Name the model subcircuit (instead of template)
*9) Copy all of template to line_coupled.lib
*10) Input previously noted Ce,CShield,R,Rshield in the model

* HINT: You can now (simpler) also use the excel file for copy pasting the atp-matrix  to excel file than to line_coupled.lib file:
* ATP_cables_and_lines.xlsx in folder ..\ltspice\loadflow_transient_examples_with_some_documentation_directly_in_asc_file\ATP_EMTP_OverheadLines_Models

* Model cable with very thick shield (only for testing) ideal shielded cable)
* NOTE: The shield currents are calculated by ATP-matrices:
* Coupled resistors of ATP-matrix not used!
* Resistor value of VERIFY command  connected in series at the input port
* Line Data for steady state: R=0.018 XL=0.02043 CB=325nF CE=325nF
* see also: ..\ltspice\loadflow_transient_examples_with_some_documentation_directly_in_asc_file\ATP_EMTP_Cables_Models
* see also: ..\ltspice\loadflow_transient_examples_with_some_documentation_directly_in_asc_file\Crossbonding
